{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "nonlinear_return_cluster",
  "intent": "Refine the parent's progress-modulated return/regret balance with nonlinear (concave) growth of the return weight so tour-closure pressure ramps faster mid-tour, and a convex decay of the regret weight so look-ahead overhead fades once local decisions suffice. Add a small decaying cluster-density bonus that rewards visiting candidates embedded in dense unvisited neighborhoods during early construction, helping clustered instances without disturbing late-stage closure.",
  "tags": [
    "nonlinear",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['return_distance']\n    g = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    c = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + (0.1 + 0.5 * p ** 0.5) * r + 0.2 * (1 - p) ** 1.5 * g + 0.1 * (1 - 0.5 * p) * c",
